```python
DEFAULT_LIMITS = {"cpu": 1, "mem": 512}

def normalise(name, *, tags=None, limits=None, region="us-east-1"):
    tags = list(tags) if tags is not None else []
    merged_limits = {**DEFAULT_LIMITS, **(limits or {})}
    return {
        "name": name,
        "tags": sorted(set(tags)),
        "limits": merged_limits,
        "region": region.lower(),
    }
```
`list(tags)` and the `{**...}` merge both copy, so the caller's objects are never touched and nothing is shared between calls.
